","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KnifeXRage","html_url":"https://github.com/KnifeXRage","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KnifeXRage/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KnifeXRage/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KnifeXRage/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KnifeXRage/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KnifeXRage/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KnifeXRage/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KnifeXRage/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KnifeXRage/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KnifeXRage/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-15T14:46:19Z","updated_at":"2025-10-15T14:46:19Z","body":"Thanks for asking! Size flags control how a child expands or fills space, but they don’t let you explicitly align content inside a `ScrollContainer`.\r\n\r\nWith the proposed `horizontal_content_align` and `vertical_content_align` properties, developers can directly position content (center, right, bottom, etc.) without adding extra nodes or writing custom scripts and it can be directly controlled using gdscript, which makes layouts simpler and more intuitive.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3406829729/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3406892817","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111680#issuecomment-3406892817","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111680","id":3406892817,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7LEQ8R","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-15T14:59:48Z","updated_at":"2025-10-15T15:00:43Z","body":"But it doesn't need any \"extra\" nodes. The ScrollContainer already requires one content node (BoxContainer, GridContainer etc.), and that node is the subject to size flags. You even have one in your video, I replicated that layout. You can set the alignment from GDScript using `set_anchors_and_offsets_preset()`.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3406892817/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3406944207","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111680#issuecomment-3406944207","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111680","id":3406944207,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7LEdfP","user":{"login":"KnifeXRage","id":172096350,"node_id":"U_kgDOCkH7Xg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/172096350?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://